      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-ds-students\" data-username=\"Shashwat1107\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"163161\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://dub1.discourse-cdn.com/flex013/user_avatar/discourse.onlinedegree.iitm.ac.in/shashwat1107/48/66894_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Shashwat1107:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Can We use the <em><strong>Window Subsystem Linux</strong></em> as my Linux system.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes, you can use WSL too. For practicing on your local PC or else even if you want to try sudo command too.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-ds-students\" data-username=\"Shashwat1107\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"163161\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://dub1.discourse-cdn.com/flex013/user_avatar/discourse.onlinedegree.iitm.ac.in/shashwat1107/48/66894_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Shashwat1107:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Or it’s necessary for future sessions to use only the VM given by the instructors?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes, it is necessary for BPT’s, VM Practice Questions and OPPE Exam.</p>",
